      "claim": "The query is a neutral, highly lipophilic N-formylleucine ester of a substituted beta-lactone with long alkyl chains (logP 6.88, MW 495.75, TPSA 81.7, 23 rotatable bonds), placing it in the poorly soluble lipophilic ester class; the most transferable direct human F measurements for such esters are low: testosterone undecanoate 6.8 ± 3.3% (C15) and 6.83 ± 3.32% vs IV (C30), oral testosterone 3.66 ± 2.45% (C13), and crystalline TU poor (C16).",
